{"card":{"card_id":"ma-c-10f1bea20018db71746b","statement":"In the Gelfand-Tsetlin formulae (<<ref:Gelfand-Tsetlin formulas>>), none of the $[l_{ki}-l_{kj}]_q$ is zero if $l_{n1}-l_{nn}\\leq e$. So when $q$ is a root of unity, Theorem <<ref:Theorem: quantum GT theorem>> holds if $\\lambda_1-\\lambda_n\\leq e+1-n$. For a generic tableau$T(L)$ all $[l_{ki}-l_{kj}]_q$ are not zero. Hence, Theorem <<ref:Theorem: GT theorem q-generic>> holds when $q$ is a root of unity.","source_id":"arXiv:1610.08126","cluster":"representation_theory","statement_sha256":"793db32996f3fc17b38d11e82aed7e68a200f91f899448b5800e15cca87f489b","kind":"remark","label":"Remark 21","ref_key":"","name":"","order":20,"deps":[{"ref":"Gelfand-Tsetlin formulas","card_id":"ma-c-2264c455e85a82046a41","label":"Equation Gelfand-Tsetlin formulas","resolved":true,"target":"card"},{"ref":"Theorem: GT theorem q-generic","card_id":"ma-c-fb97a8d2aeed8ee8f4f0","label":"Theorem 10","resolved":true,"target":"card"},{"ref":"Theorem: quantum GT theorem","card_id":"ma-c-ffb0765865bf77eed6ee","label":"Theorem 6","resolved":true,"target":"card"}],"cite_keys":[],"provenance":{"source_url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1610.08126","harvest_mode":"arxiv_eprint","payload_sha256":"f34fb91ab9fa176f2125d51ecafd84d216a0abfb09f46d58023d7396533e0750","line":582,"origin":"latex_env","retrieved_at":"2026-09-29T14:14:11+08:00"},"wash":{"version":"cardwash.v3","stages":["segment","purify","classify","dedupe","emit"],"numbering":"document_order_with_label_heuristic","detail":{"stripped_proof":false,"chars":405,"math_hints":24}}},"paper":{"source_id":"arXiv:1610.08126","title":"Irreducible subquotients of generic Gelfand-Tsetlin modules over $U_{q}(\\mathfrak{gl}_n)$","abstract":"We provide a classification and explicit bases of tableaux of all irreducible subquotients of generic Gelfand-Tsetlin modules over Uq(gl(n)) where q different 1 and -1.","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Enrique Ramirez","Jian Zhang"],"year":"2016","url":"https://arxiv